  "reason": "Evidence: With concat fusion, avgpool aggregation outperformed transformer by ~4% (0.619 vs 0.579), and weighted fusion outperformed concat by ~2% (0.639 vs 0.619) under avgpool. However, the aggregation×fusion interaction is untested: we do not know whether the avgpool>transformer gap persists when fusion is weighted. Question: Does transformer aggregation remain inferior under weighted fusion, or does weighted fusion partially compensate for the weaker aggregation? Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most direct logical extension of the two strongest findings (avgpool superiority and weighted superiority), it cleanly isolates the aggregation variable in the context of the best-performing fusion strategy, and its result will determine whether transformer can be ruled out entirely for all remaining experiments—saving budget from exploring a potentially dead branch. If transformer+weighted is also clearly worse, we can confidently focus all subsequent experiments on avgpool variants and new encoders; if it is competitive, it reveals an important interaction that changes the search strategy."
